{
  "notes": {
    "bigquery": "jobs.query runs any SQL, including DML and DDL, so it is classified write. Its tool is registered only when GSM_ALLOW_WRITES=true. Check the statement before running it.",
    "indexing": "Only for pages with JobPosting or BroadcastEvent (inside VideoObject) structured data. Google restricts this API to those page types.",
    "secretmanager": "versions.access returns the secret payload in clear text. Treat the output as a credential.",
    "tagmanager": "versions.publish makes a container version live, which changes tags on live sites.",
    "script": "scripts.run executes Apps Script code with the project's authority, so it is classified destructive.",
    "compute": "Methods that remove, detach, stop or suspend resources are classified write unless listed as destructive. Check the effect first.",
    "cloudidentity": "devices.wipe factory-resets the device and is destructive.",
    "sqladmin": "instances.export writes a dump file to Cloud Storage. It is classified write.",
    "googleads": "Every mutate method is dynamic, so the risk is decided per call from the body. validateOnly true is a read and is not gated; a remove operation is destructive; any other operation is a write. The rule is the same in the per-method tools, the gateway and the hook (src/core/dynamic.ts)."
  },
